title: Sign-in, token refresh and signed file links
participant U "User (browser SPA)"
participant A "API: auth module"
participant M "API: any module"
participant D "PostgreSQL"
== Sign-in ==
U -> A: POST /api/auth/login {username, password} (rate limit 10 / 5 min per IP and per username)
A -> D: load user, roles, permissions; bcrypt compare
note: Wrong password: failed_logins + 1, account locked at limits.max_login_attempts (5). 2FA users get a 5-minute challenge token and call POST /auth/login/2fa with the TOTP code. must_change_password or an expired password yields a restricted token that only reaches change-password.
A -> D: insert refresh_tokens (jti, family, expiry 30 days); login_history row
A --> U: accessToken (HS256, 30 min, sub, roles, permissions, tv = token_version) + refreshToken (jti)
== Every API call ==
U -> M: Authorization: Bearer access token
M -> D: users.status = active AND token_version = tv ?
M --> U: 200 data (file URLs signed ?exp=&sig=, valid FILE_URL_TTL_SECONDS = 30 min) or 401
== Access token expired ==
U -> A: POST /api/auth/refresh {refreshToken} (one shared refresh per tab; fetch wrapper + axios interceptor)
A -> D: token live and not revoked? revoke old jti (rotated), issue new pair in the same family
note: A rotated refresh token presented again after the grace window is treated as theft: the whole family is revoked, the event is audited and recorded in login_history. Password change / reset, deactivation and role changes raise token_version (and revoke refresh tokens), ending every session.
A --> U: new access + refresh token; SPA retries the original request
== Sign-out ==
U -> A: POST /api/auth/logout {refreshToken}
A -> D: revoke refresh token (reason logout)
